  "description": "EfficientNet-B0 pretrained backbone with 1\u21923 channel expansion, SpecAugment (freq_mask=24, time_mask=48, 2 masks each), mixup \u03b1=0.4, focal loss (\u03b3=2, \u03b1=0.75) for long-tail, dropout 0.4 before 206-unit sigmoid head, cosine-annealing LR schedule from 1e-3 to 1e-5 over 30 epochs, AdamW weight_decay=1e-4.",
  "reasoning": "The best result so far (0.4486) used efficientnet_b0 with mixup and heavy dropout. To push further, I add focal loss to address the long-tail minority classes that are the hard case, combine SpecAugment for stronger regularization on spectrograms, and use cosine annealing for smoother convergence. These are complementary improvements targeting the exact weakness (minority class recall) while staying within the same proven backbone family."
